  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs` `impl[UnreadContents/NodeContents]/fn[fingerprint]` meets the built-in's criteria.\n\n- **Form:** the justification is in fenced `:::{cite}` commentary inside the item's assessed input. It is not a bare non-doc comment.\n- **Substance:** the reason is that the type is uninhabited, so no value exists and no call can reach the body. The body is `match *self {}`, which has no arm to run. This is a real reason, not just difficulty.\n- **Agreement with the source:** `enum[UnreadContents]` is declared as `enum UnreadContents {}`, which has no variants. So the claim that no value can be constructed and no content method can be called is correct. `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/type[NodeContent]` sets `NodeContent = UnreadContents`, which supports the claim that the impl exists to satisfy the `Domain` associated-type bound. I did not read the `Domain` trait declaration to confirm that bound.\n- **Scope:** the citation is on an explicit function with a body, which is the case where the exception excuses a recorded zero execution.",
